  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Targets .NET 10 (net10.0) instead of .NET 9. Projects on .NET 8 or 9 should stay on 0.0.0.5.\n\t\t\tNo public API changes since 0.0.0.5.\n\t\t\tOfflineFileSources now reads its CSV file as a stream through the NHSISL.CsvHelperClient 3.x API, with the same results. This also fixes the MissingMethodException that OfflineFileSources 0.0.0.5 throws in projects that use NHSISL.CsvHelperClient 3.x.\n\t\t\tDependency changes: Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection 9.0.2 to 10.0.13, Xeption 2.8.0 to 2.9.0 and, in Necs, RESTFulSense 3.1.0 to 3.2.0. FluentAssertions is now pinned to exactly 7.2.2 (it was 7.0.0 or later). DemoData and OfflineFileSources move NHSISL.CsvHelperClient from 1.1.0 to 3.1.0, a major version, so projects that reference NHSISL.CsvHelperClient 1.x directly need to move to 3.x as well.\n\t\t\tThe package license changes from MIT to Apache 2.0.",
